  "limitations": [
    "Preserve signed kg of water delivered at the user with factor +1, including uncertainty, formulas and caller ownership. The source reference is not a cubic-metre withdrawal, dry material or treatment-only service. Do not apply a kg-to-litre/m3 factor or multiply by source water-production or distribution-loss coefficients.",
    "Use the complete native Swiss tap-water inventory once, including abstraction, treatment chemicals, electricity, water works, pump/storage/network infrastructure, internal logistics, wastewater and its own water balance. Preserve separately listed caller water, transport and emissions; add no duplicate network, water withdrawal or treatment step.",
    "The source markets use different treatment mixes and distribution losses. The native record is documented as a rough Swiss estimation. Source Europe-without-Switzerland, RoW and South-African supply conditions, water-resource geography, network losses, energy and infrastructure are not reconstructed. Regionalized water-stress or LCIA equivalence is not established and score effects are unquantified.",
